|    = {CG: -1, CJ: 1, DI: 1, DE: -1}
We are left with a linear equation with coefficients {CG: -1, CJ: 1, DI: 1, DE: -1} that gives ∠(CG,CJ) = ∠(DI,DE)



020. | Angle Chasing to prove ∠(CG,CJ) = ∠(GI,IJ):
