| Then {AC: 1, CG: -1, GI: 1, CJ: 1, IJ: -2} + -1 x {AC: 1, IJ: -1}
|    = {CG: -1, GI: 1, CJ: 1, IJ: -1}
We are left with a linear equation with coefficients {CG: -1, GI: 1, CJ: 1, IJ: -1} that gives ∠(CG,CJ) = ∠(GI,IJ)



024. | Angle Chasing to prove ∠(CG,GJ) = ∠(DI,EI):
| Premise ∠(AB,AI) = ∠(AI,AC) gives a linear equation with coefficients {AB: -1, AC: -1, AI: 2}
